    "answer": {
      "short": "Sample answers: $1.023$, $1.032$, $1.203$, $1.230$, $1.302$, $1.320$, $2.013$, $2.031$, $2.103$, $2.130$.",
      "worked": "Keep one digit before the decimal point and arrange the other three after it. With $1$ before the point, the six arrangements are $1.023$, $1.032$, $1.203$, $1.230$, $1.302$ and $1.320$. Four further examples with $2$ before the point are $2.013$, $2.031$, $2.103$ and $2.130$. These ten numbers are different, and each uses all four digits exactly once.",
